var e=[{id:`faq-who`,question:"Do I need experience to start?",answer:"No. Plenty of people start without ever having touched a barbell. We start where you are, and your plan grows with you."},{id:`faq-frequency`,question:"How often should I train?",answer:"Most people do well with 2 to 4 sessions a week. We decide together, based on your goal and your schedule."},{id:`faq-online`,question:"What is the difference between personal training and online coaching?",answer:"With personal training, I'm next to you in the gym. With online coaching, you train on your own and I guide you with a plan in your client dashboard, a weekly check-in and feedback on your videos."},{id:`faq-gym`,question:"Do I need a gym membership?",answer:"Most programs are made for a regular gym, but training at home is possible too. Tell me what equipment you have and I'll build the plan around it."},{id:`faq-results`,question:"How quickly will I see results?",answer:"That depends on where you start, how consistently you train and eat, how well you sleep, and your body. Most people notice they're getting stronger before they see a change in the mirror. No honest coach can promise a specific result or date."},{id:`faq-nutrition`,question:"Do you help with food and diet?",answer:"Yes, with practical guidance that fits your training: calorie and macro targets and a simple meal structure. Detailed meal plans are part of the Premium and Contest Prep packages. For a medical diet, please see a dietitian."},{id:`faq-cancel`,question:"Can I pause or cancel?",answer:"Monthly packages can be cancelled before the next billing date. If a package has a minimum term, it's stated on the pricing page and in the terms of service."},{id:`faq-medical`,question:"Can I train with you if I have an injury?",answer:"Tell me about it first. I can adapt exercises, but I'm not a doctor or physiotherapist. If needed, I'll ask you to get a green light from your doctor before we start."},{id:`faq-supplements`,question:"Do I need supplements?",answer:"No. Training, food, sleep and consistency do the work. A few well-researched supplements, like creatine monohydrate, can help a little. I'm happy to explain what the research says."}];export{e as t};